---
title: Aloo Gobi
description: A dry North Indian stir-fry of potatoes and cauliflower cooked with onion, tomato and ground spices until the potatoes are soft and the cauliflower keeps a slight bite.
author: Swasthi Shreekanth
source: https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/aloo-gobi-recipe/
course: main
cuisine: indian
diet: vegan
difficulty: easy
servings: 3
time: 50m
prep time: 15m
cook time: 35m
tags: [potato, cauliflower, stir-fried]
---

= Preparation =

Cut the @cauliflower florets{180%g} into pieces of about 4 cm. Put them in a #bowl of slightly hot water for ~{3%minutes}, then drain, rinse well and drain completely.

Peel the @potatoes{2} and cut into 2 cm cubes. Keep them submerged in water until needed; they absorb a little moisture and cook faster.

Finely chop the @onion{1} and @green chilli{1}. Deseed and finely chop the @tomatoes{2}. Mince or grate the @ginger{1%cm} and @garlic cloves{3}.

= Cooking =

Heat @oil{2%tbsp} in a #heavy-bottomed pan with lid{}. Add @cumin seeds{0.5%tsp}; when they sizzle, add the ginger and garlic and sauté for ~{30%seconds}.

Add the onion and green chilli and fry until the onion turns translucent.

Drain the potatoes, add them to the pan and stir-fry for ~{2%minutes}. Cover and cook over low to medium heat, stirring now and then, until they are about half done, ~{8%minutes}. If they start to dry out, sprinkle in a few spoonfuls of @water{3%tbsp}.

Add the cauliflower and stir-fry ~{3%minutes}. Add @Kashmiri chilli powder{1%tsp}, @turmeric{0.25%tsp}, @roasted cumin powder{0.5%tsp}, @garam masala{1%tsp} and @coriander powder{1%tsp} and mix well.

Sprinkle a little more water over the vegetables and around the sides of the pan to keep the dish from drying out. Cover and cook on low heat, stirring every few minutes, until both potatoes and cauliflower are almost fork-tender, ~{8%minutes}.

Add @salt{0.5%tsp}, cover again and cook on low until the potatoes are fully soft, ~{5%minutes}. Watch the cauliflower closely here: the vegetables release moisture and cook quickly, and the cauliflower should stay slightly crunchy.

Add the tomatoes. Crush @kasuri methi{1%tbsp} between your palms over the pan. Fry on medium-high heat until the raw smell of the tomatoes is gone, ~{2%minutes}, adding a splash of oil if it sticks. Taste and adjust salt and spices.

Sprinkle over @amchur{0.5%tsp}, garnish with @coriander leaves{2%tbsp}, finely chopped, and add @lemon juice{to serve} if you like. Serve hot with rice or roti.

> Don't add salt or tomatoes until the potatoes are nearly cooked: with so little water in the pan, both slow the potatoes down.

> Keeps 2 to 3 days in the fridge. Reheat in a wide pan or the oven.

-- Covered cooking times after adding the spices are estimated; the source gives none.